  "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={e}^{x}\\,{|}_{2}^{5} \\\\  & ={e}^{5}-{e}^{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{5}-{e}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
